        <obo:IAO_0000028>PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tns1 (Mmus), Unc5d (Mmus), Otp (Mmus), Cadps2 (Mmus), Pdyn (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Subclass:133 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>133 PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>152 PVH-SO-PVa_Otp:Fezf2_Glut</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hypothalamus (HY; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: neuron of the forebrain; hypothalamus cell. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>PVH-SO-PVa Otp Glut glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
