        <obo:IAO_0000028>PAG Pou4f1 Ebf2 Glut (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lrrtm4 (Mmus), D130079A08Rik (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus), Kit (Mmus), Barhl1 (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Subclass:172 PAG Pou4f1 Ebf2 Glut.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>172 PAG Pou4f1 Ebf2 Glut</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>195 PAG_Pou4f1:Barhl1:Adamtsl1_Glut</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Periaqueductal gray (PAG; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>PAG Pou4f1 Ebf2 Glut glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>https://knowledge.brain-map.org/abcatlas#AQIBQVA4Sk5ONUxZQUJHVk1HS1kxQgACUTFOQ1dXUEc2RlowRE5JWEpCUQADBAFGUzAwRFhWMFQ5UjFYOUZKNFFFAAIAAAFRWTVTOEtNTzVITEpVRjBQMDBLAAIBMTcyIFBBRyBQb3U0ZjEgRWJmMiBHbHV0AAABMTVCSzQ3RENJT0YxU0xMVVc5UAACAAABQ0JHQzBVMzBWVjlKUFI2MFRKVQACAAAEAQECgazGjoGWFSADhGpN%%2BAAAABAAACFZGT0ZZUEZRR1JLVURRVVozRkYACUxWREJKQVc4Qkk1WVNTMVFVQkcACgALAVRMT0tXQ0w5NVJVMDNEOVBFVEcAAjczR1ZURFhERUdFMjdNMlhKTVQAAwEEAQACIzAwMDAwMAADyAEABQEBAiMwMDAwMDAAA8gBAAAAAgMA</rdfs:seeAlso>
