        <owl:annotatedTarget>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Hypothalamus (HY; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter histamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: neuron of the forebrain; hypothalamus cell. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, TMv-PMv Tbx3 Hist-Gaba_1 does not have cells in tuberomammillary nucleus, ventral part (TMv). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</owl:annotatedTarget>
