        <owl:annotatedTarget>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Midbrain (MB; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter dopamine (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: region+NT. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_4 does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06808-9</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
