        <obo:IAO_0000028>LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Nfib Glut_1 (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nkx6-1 (Mmus), Gpc4 (Mmus), Pou6f2 (Mmus), Nfib (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:0948 LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Nfib Glut_1.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>0948 LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Nfib Glut_1</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>0948 LDT-PCG_Vsx2:Pax5_Glut 2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Nfib Glut_1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for laterodorsal tegmental nucleus (LDT). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>LDT Vsx2 Nkx6-1 Nfib Glut_1 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
