        <obo:IAO_0000028>SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Fn1 (Mmus), Clec1a (Mmus). Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Supertype:1017 SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut_1.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1003 SPVO_Tlx3:Mafa:Fn1_Glut 1</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1017 SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut_1</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>255 SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Medulla (MY; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter glutamate (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>SPVO Mafa Meis2 Glut glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
