        <obo:IAO_0000028>CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5 Nxph4 (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glutamatergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Crispld2 (Mmus), Slc5a7 (Mmus), Glp1r (Mmus), Nxph4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5 cells by expression of Nxph4, Ebf2. It is glutamatergic (inferred from expression of Slc17a6). These cells are located in the Midbrain, Pons , in or close to the regions: Nucleus sagulum, Nucleus of the lateral lemniscus, lateral lemniscus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3351 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>3351 CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>4636 CUN-PPN_Evx2:Bnc2_Glut 2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5 Nxph4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for cuneiform nucleus (CUN), pedunculopontine nucleus (PPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>CUN-PPN Evx2 Meis2 Glut_5 Nxph4 glutamatergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
