        <obo:IAO_0000028>SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3 Mob3b (Mmus)</obo:IAO_0000028>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A GABAergic neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pax7 (Mmus), Bmpr1b (Mmus), Lncenc1 (Mmus), Pou6f2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Mob3b. It is GABAergic (inferred from expression of Gad2, Gad1, Slc32a1). These cells are located in the Midbrain , in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Superior colliculus, motor related, deep gray layer, Inferior colliculus, dorsal nucleus . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:3694 SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>3694 SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>4096 SC-PAG_Lef1:Emx2_Gaba 2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: Despite its name, SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3 Mob3b does not have cells in periaqueductal gray (PAG). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>SC-PAG Lef1 Emx2 Gaba_3 Mob3b GABAergic neuron (Mmus)</rdfs:label>
