        <rdfs:comment>Rationale for assigning this type to reference data: Assigned by automated classification (ELK) of a definition built from soma location Pons (P; ≥80% of grey-matter cells in both the Yao 2023 and Zhuang 2023 MERFISH atlases) and neurotransmitter serotonin (all clusters) against CL 2026-06-08. Basis: NT. Other inferred CL parents: central nervous system neuron. [WMBO CL promotion round 1, 2026-10-13] Location is inferred from registration of MerFish Data. Registration may be inaccurate, giving misleading location to adjacent anatomical regions. Warning: This type MB-MY Tph2 Glut-Sero_7 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for midbrain (MB), medulla (MY). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.</rdfs:comment>
